// percentage (gradual rollout) or a measured split (A/B test). Design: forge
// docs/proposals/changes.md.
//
// THE RELEASE DECLARES WHAT A CHANGE CAN BE; THIS SERVICE DECIDES WHO GETS
// IT. A change's variants and default are declared in the project's
// changes.yaml and ship in the environment's release shape (`changes` key).
// Launching, ramping or rolling out a variant the environment's CURRENT
// release does not declare is refused (FailedPrecondition, reason
// "change_not_declared" / "variant_not_declared"). Drafts, previews and Stop
// are allowed against an undeclared change, so a team can prepare a change
// before the release that declares it ships.
//
// WHO MAY DO WHAT. Every rpc names its environment or change; a caller who is
// not a member of the environment's org, or a credential of another org,
// gets NotFound, so ids are no existence oracle.
//   - reads (List/Get/ListChangeEvents/GetChangesDeliveryStatus): any org
//     member; a token carrying changes:write, changes:launch or obs:read.
//   - GetChangesSnapshot: a read, and also a token carrying changes:read
//     (org-wide, or bound to that environment): the credential of an app
//     not on Reliant hosting, which fetches the snapshot it evaluates. That
//     scope reads the snapshot and NOTHING ELSE: every other rpc, the reads
//     included, refuses a token whose only Changes authority is changes:read
//     (PermissionDenied, reason "scope_missing").
//   - GetChangeReadout: a read, and obs:read (every member holds it; a token
//     must carry it).
//   - CreateChange, UpdateChangeDraft, SetChangePreview, StopChange,
//     RequestChangeApproval: changes:write (org-wide or bound to the env).
//   - LaunchChange, RampChange, RollOutChange, EndChangeRun: changes:launch
//     (which implies changes:write).
//
// A PERSON APPROVES PRODUCTION. In a protected environment (protected, or
// named prod / production) a launch, a ramp UP, a roll-out, and therefore any
// change to a running experiment, needs a person: the request comes from a
// browser session of the console, or carries step_up_code, a one-time code
// RequestChangeApproval emailed to the person the credential acts for. A CLI
// login or a token acting as a person (what an agent holds) is not, by
// itself, a person's approval. Ramping DOWN, EndChangeRun and StopChange never
// need approval: reducing exposure never waits for anyone. A refusal is
// PermissionDenied, reason "approval_required".
//
// OPTIMISTIC CONCURRENCY. Every mutation names expected_revision, the change's
// revision the caller read, and bumps it by one; a stale one is
